l\/7.4.308","article-title":"A simplex method for function minimization","volume":"7","author":"Nelder","year":"1965","journal-title":"Comput. J."},{"key":"B11","unstructured":"Proximal policy optimization"},{"key":"B12","unstructured":"Soft actor-critic"},{"key":"B13","unstructured":"Algorithm\n          \n          \n          2023"},{"key":"B14","unstructured":"Algorithm\n          \n          \n          2023"},{"key":"B15","unstructured":"Algorithm\n          \n          \n          2023"},{"key":"B16","unstructured":"Reaction wheel scenario\n          \n          \n            \n              Schaub\n              H.\n            \n          \n          \n          2023"},{"key":"B17","volume-title":"Analytical mechanics of space systems","author":"Schaub","year":"2018"},{"key":"B18","volume-title":"Proximal policy optimization","author":"Schulman","year":"2017"},{"key":"B19","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1360","DOI":"10.1109\/ACC.2002.1023210","article-title":"Spacecraft robust attitude tracking design: pid control approach","volume-title":"Proceedings of the 2002 American control conference (IEEE cat. No.CH37301) 2","author":"Show","year":"2002"},{"key":"B20","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"1","DOI":"10.1016\/j.arcontrol.2022.07.004","article-title":"Reinforcement learning in spacecraft control applications: advances, prospects, and challenges","volume":"54","author":"Tipaldi","year":"2022","journal-title":"Annu. Rev. Control"},{"key":"B21","volume-title":"Fundamentals of astrodynamics and applications","author":"Vallado","year":"2001"},{"key":"B22","unstructured":"Vizard\n          \n          \n          2023"},{"key":"B23","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","first-page":"0047","DOI":"10.34133\/space.0047","article-title":"Optimal multi-impulse linear rendezvous via reinforcement learning","volume":"3","author":"Xu","year":"2023","journal-title":"Space Sci. Technol."}],"container-title":["Frontiers in Robotics and AI"],"link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/www.frontiersin.org\/articles\/10.3389\/frobt.2024.1402846\/full","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,23]],"date-time":"2024-07-23T01:10:30Z","timestamp":1721697030000},"score":36.247265,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.frontiersin.org\/articles\/10.3389\/frobt.2024.1402846\/full"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,23]]},"references-count":23,"alternative-id":["10.3389\/frobt.2024.1402846"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3389\/frobt.2024.1402846","ISSN":["2296-9144"],"issn-type":[{"value":"2296-9144","type":"electronic"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2024,7,23]]},"article-number":"1402846"},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,3,24]],"date-time":"2026-03-24T16:22:17Z","timestamp":1774369337211,"version":"3.50.1"},"reference-count":24,"publisher":"Emerald","issue":"3","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,20]],"date-time":"2019-05-20T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1558310400000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/www.emerald.com\/insight\/site-policies"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["IR"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2019,5,20]]},"abstract":"<jats:sec>\n<jats:title content-type=\"abstract-subheading\">Purpose<\/jats:title>\n<jats:p>Recently, deep reinforcement learning is developing rapidly and shows its power to solve difficult problems such as robotics and game of GO. Meanwhile, satellite attitude control systems are still using classical control technics such as proportional \u2013 integral \u2013 derivative and slide mode control as major solutions, facing problems with adaptability and automation.<\/jats:p>\n<\/jats:sec>\n<jats:sec>\n<jats:title content-type=\"abstract-subheading\">Design\/methodology\/approach<\/jats:title>\n<jats:p>In this paper, an approach based on deep reinforcement learning is proposed to increase adaptability and autonomy of satellite control system. It is a model-based algorithm which could find solutions with fewer episodes of learning than model-free algorithms.<\/jats:p>\n<\/jats:sec>\n<jats:sec>\n<jats:title content-type=\"abstract-subheading\">Findings<\/jats:title>\n<jats:p>Simulation experiment shows that when classical control crashed, this approach could find solution and reach the target with hundreds times of explorations and learning.<\/jats:p>\n<\/jats:sec>\n<jats:sec>\n<jats:title content-type=\"abstract-subheading\">Originality\/value<\/jats:title>\n<jats:p>This approach is a non-gradient method using heuristic search to optimize policy to avoid local optima. Compared with classical control technics, this approach does not need prior knowledge of satellite or its orbit, has the ability to adapt different kinds of situations with data learning and has the ability to adapt different kinds of satellite and different tasks through transfer learning.<\/jats:p>\n<\/jats:sec>","DOI":"10.1108\/ir-05-2018-0086","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2018,10,16]],"date-time":"2018-10-16T05:50:28Z","timestamp":1539669028000},"page":"415-420","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":5,"title":["Model-based deep reinforcement learning with heuristic search for satellite attitude control"],"prefix":"10.1108","volume":"46","author":[{"given":"Ke","family":"Xu","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Fengge","family":"Wu","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"Junsuo","family":"Zhao","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"140","reference":[{"key":"key2019090415305321900_ref001","article-title":"Tensorflow: large-scale machine learning on heterogeneous distributed systems","year":"2016"},{"key":"key2019090415305321900_ref002","first-page":"442","article-title":"Partial lyapunov strictification: smooth angular v